# Files markdownlint must not gate on.
#
# Honoured automatically by markdownlint-cli (v1) — the CI `lint` job and
# the lint-on-write hook both use it, so this file is the single source of
# truth and CI needs no duplicate --ignore flags.
# NOTE: markdownlint-cli2 does NOT read this file. If you switch to cli2,
# re-express these entries as `ignores` in .markdownlint-cli2.jsonc.

node_modules
target
dist

# --- Generated: nobody authored these, and nobody can fix them ----------
#
# release-please writes CHANGELOG.md with two blank lines between
# sections; MD012/no-multiple-blanks wants one. That failure surfaces on
# the release PR — the most expensive possible moment, since branch
# protection then blocks the release on a file no human can edit.
CHANGELOG.md
docs/api/
coverage/

# --- Agent-facing templates --------------------------------------------
#
# plinth/ ships NLSpec scaffolds whose table of contents links to
# <Placeholder> headings. Those anchors cannot resolve until the
# placeholders are filled in (MD051), and the instructional blocks use
# indented bullets inside <...> prose (MD007/MD032). Linting them means
# mangling authoring guidance to satisfy rules aimed at finished docs.
#
# Once your specs are filled in, narrow this to `plinth/planning/` to put
# plinth/specs/ back under the linter.
plinth/
